// Quazi self-host compiler — design scaffold, NOT implementation.
// Component: semantic.types
// File: checking.qz
// Responsibility: Type checking.
// Package boundary: Resolution, types, ownership and validation of Quazi semantics.
// TODO(P0/P1): implement existing bootstrap behavior with clean interfaces.
// Do not introduce new language features before bootstrap parity.
// Split boundary: this file remains the coordinator for its responsibility;
// implementation details belong to the adjacent modules listed below.
//   types/check/expressions.qz: Type-checking expression forms, including contextual expected types; delegate specialized cases.
//   types/check/items.qz: Type-checking item declarations, function bodies, parameters and declared signatures.
//   types/check/calls.qz: Checking function/method calls, arguments, overload resolution and generic call instantiation.
//   types/check/operators.qz: Unary/binary operator type rules, numeric compatibility and return types.
//   types/check/compatibility.qz: Assignment/return type compatibility and implicit or explicit coercion checks.
